  "reason": "The best result so far is config_005 (scvi_n200, multiprofile, avgpool) at 0.650 accuracy. For pca_n2000, avgpool (0.591) clearly beat transformer (0.519), but scvi_n200 produces a fundamentally different latent representation that may interact differently with attention-based aggregation. config_006 isolates the aggregation effect for the best-performing encoder, directly extending the top result. This is the highest-value next experiment because: (1) it exploits the strongest evidence (scvi_n200 + multiprofile), (2) it answers whether avgpool is truly optimal or whether transformer could push accuracy higher, and (3) the answer directly informs which aggregation to pair with scvi_n200 in any multimodal fusion experiments in the remaining 3 slots. Testing scgpt in multiprofile (config_008) is lower priority since scgpt was already weaker than pca in singleprofile (0.411 vs 0.485), making it unlikely to surpass scvi_n200."
